 "provenance": {
  "chassis": {
   "confidence": "datasheet",
   "note": "1RU, 440 x 44 x 360 - the data sheet's \"44 cm x 36 cm x 4.4 cm\", \"1U, 19-inch rack-mountable\", 4.47 kg. The rack ears are not part of the face."
  },
  "front-layout": {
   "confidence": "photo-measured",
   "note": "POSITIONS ARE THE RENDER'S. It is square-on across and seen from above, so the face is 136 px tall where its 1504 px width says 150; rectifying the four face corners (105.5,394 1609.5,394 1609.5,530 105.5,530) onto the data sheet's 440 x 44 takes the foreshortening out, and every cage, jack, lamp, vent and legend is placed from dark-run and centroid scans of that 10 px/mm image. The stencil master is used for the arrangement and legends only."
  },
  "lamps": {
   "confidence": "photo-measured",
   "note": "LNK/ACT and SPEED are two lamps each (318.4 and 328.8 across, 29.3 and 34.95 down) under bracketed legends; which ports they report is not documented - presumably the two QSFPs, upper and lower. Six status lamps in two columns (416.8 and 423.9) under stacked legends PWR1 / FAN1 / SNMP and PWR2 / FAN2 / SYS, read top to bottom. No document says what any state means."
  },
  "model": {
   "confidence": "datasheet",
   "note": "XM-8102 data sheet (telco.com 2026-08); the faceplate prints X-METRO 8102."
  },
  "ports": {
   "confidence": "photo-measured",
   "note": "The 24 SFP+ ports are two stacked 2 x 6 blocks, std/sfp-ganged@1, upper row bail up and lower row turned 180, on the measured 14.45 and 14.61 pitches (columns 19.55-91.8 and 117.3-190.35, rows 14.15 and 32.15); the strip between the rows carries two arrow lamps per port, down-up-down-up, at the XM-8424H's and TM-3312's offsets from the column centre (-4.75, -1.9, +1.8, +4.65; measured here -4.55, -1.55, +1.95, +4.75 - within 0.35 mm, about 1.2 px of the source render). Each column is legended with one pair, 2/1 to 24/23; the upper cage is drawn as the first number (see the port-order gap). THE NUMERALS ARE PLACED WHERE PRINTED, measured by clustering their glyphs: they run on a 14.29 and a 14.44 pitch against the cages' 14.45 and 14.61, so they sit 1.85 mm right of the first column and drift to 0.1 mm right of the last, and L61 stays in the baseline for them on purpose. A column of five vent dots stands at the left of each block. QSFP 1 and 2 are a 1 x 2 row (std/qsfp-ganged@1 at 231.25 and 261.35) under a bracketed \"40GE/100GE\" legend."
  },
  "power": {
   "confidence": "datasheet",
   "note": "\"2 hot-swappable AC/DC power supplies provide 1+1 redundancy\", \"AC:220V, 100~240VAC | DC: -48V, -36~-72V\". The front carries no supply, so the supplies (and presumably the fans) are at the rear, which nothing held shows; no consumption figure is published."
  },
  "snmp-jack": {
   "confidence": "photo-measured",
   "note": "THE SNMP JACK IS BARE. At 12x the rectified render shows a metal-shielded RJ45 with no lamp windows - the two blocks in its lower corners are shield tabs, not lenses - so it is std/rj45@2, and L76 (an Ethernet jack on a part with no lamps) stays in the baseline for it on purpose, as for the S9110-32X's out-of-band jack."
  },
  "snmp-speed": {
   "confidence": "borrowed",
   "note": "BORROWED, NOT STATED. The data sheet lists \"CLI, SNMP, REST API\" and gives no rate for the SNMP (out-of-band) port; 1g is taken from the TM-8104's OOB port on the maintainer's ruling for unstated management rates; the snmp-speed gap stays open."
  },
  "sources": {
   "confidence": "datasheet",
   "note": "The data sheet (2026-08), the vendor render telco.com 2024/10/XM-8102@2x-1.png (1716 px, square-on, seen from slightly above, about 3.4 px/mm on the face), and the NetZoom stencil \"BATM X-Series\" (2025-03-07), master X-Metro 8102 (CF). No installation guide is public."
  }
 },
